WEBVTT

00:04.440 --> 00:06.900
<i>When I was in grade school,</i>

00:06.900 --> 00:09.980
<i>I was a gloomy, sullen, unpleasant child.</i>

00:10.730 --> 00:14.200
<i>And because of that, 
I didn't have any friends.</i>

00:14.700 --> 00:16.070
Ko-chan?

00:17.620 --> 00:21.370
Your cousin, Carol-chan, 
is here to play with you.

00:21.370 --> 00:23.540
She's as pretty as a little angel!

00:23.790 --> 00:28.130
Adults are always so quick to 
describe little kids as "angels."

00:28.130 --> 00:31.010
Oh, honey, do you have to be like that?

00:46.690 --> 00:48.060
Hello.

00:50.570 --> 00:51.730
<i>She's...</i>

00:53.320 --> 00:54.650
<i>an actual angel.</i>

01:10.750 --> 01:16.050
<i>When I throw a jab or a straight,
 it always lands</i>

01:16.050 --> 01:21.180
<i>But when I'm aiming for your heart,
 I miss every time</i>

01:21.180 --> 01:26.520
<i>Parallel, zigzagging, awkward, incoherent</i>

01:26.520 --> 01:31.020
<i>When you look my way and move closer to me</i>

01:31.020 --> 01:36.780
<i>I know it doesn't mean the same thing for you</i>

01:36.780 --> 01:41.830
<i>But I wish we could stay like this forever</i>

01:41.830 --> 01:47.960
<i>My changing feelings are driving me crazy</i>

01:47.960 --> 01:53.250
<i>The moment you turn to face me,
 take that! Telepathy</i>

01:53.250 --> 01:58.720
<i>If only we could feel the same thing</i>

01:58.720 --> 02:03.600
<i>I want to kick this pesky subtlety away</i>

02:03.600 --> 02:09.600
<i>I want to know everything, 
I want to know everything</i>

02:09.600 --> 02:12.150
<i>I can't fool you forever</i>

02:12.150 --> 02:14.780
<i>I can't keep this hidden</i>

02:14.780 --> 02:19.530
<i>I want to shout out my secret, AHHH</i>

02:21.450 --> 02:23.990
<i>Take that! Telepathy</i>

02:23.990 --> 02:26.450
<i>Te-te-te-telepathy</i>

02:27.160 --> 02:29.540
<i>Telepathy</i>

02:31.250 --> 02:35.000
<b>The Angel's</b>

02:31.250 --> 02:35.000
<b>True Face</b>

02:31.920 --> 02:33.630
"The Angel's True Face."

02:36.010 --> 02:37.760
I-It's good to meet you!

02:38.970 --> 02:40.550
I'm Misaki Kosuke!

02:40.840 --> 02:44.350
I admire your resolve to get stronger.

02:44.350 --> 02:45.140
Thank you!

02:45.430 --> 02:49.140
He said he wanted to join the dojo, 
but I didn't think he really would.

02:49.690 --> 02:51.650
But you are clearly...

02:53.060 --> 02:54.230
weak.

02:54.820 --> 02:56.570
You think so, too?!

02:56.570 --> 02:57.530
No, wait.

02:58.780 --> 03:01.160
I see something more behind the weakness.

03:01.610 --> 03:03.530
Wh-What is it?

03:07.370 --> 03:09.620
There's an evil spirit lurking in your soul.

03:10.290 --> 03:12.210
You had best be careful.

03:12.750 --> 03:14.080
Oh...

03:14.080 --> 03:15.790
<i>That's my dad for you.</i>

03:16.210 --> 03:18.420
Senpai, we'll start with running!

03:18.920 --> 03:20.130
Osu!

03:25.680 --> 03:28.680
We're only going up and 
down 200 little steps!

03:31.980 --> 03:33.560
Next is strength training.

03:33.560 --> 03:35.110
Three sets of fifty push-ups!

03:36.020 --> 03:38.320
You haven't pushed up once yet!

03:38.780 --> 03:41.320
Senpai, you'll be having a match next!

03:41.320 --> 03:43.570
R-Right now?!

03:43.570 --> 03:47.580
"Train in extremes" is 
our motto at this dojo.

03:47.910 --> 03:51.750
Your opponent isn't gonna care 
what kind of condition you're in.

03:52.120 --> 03:53.580
Your first opponent...

03:54.170 --> 03:55.500
will be me.

03:57.630 --> 03:59.630
<i>My first battle with Jun-kun...</i>

04:00.090 --> 04:03.010
<i>I want him to face me seriously.</i>

04:04.930 --> 04:08.600
If I can beat you in this fight...

04:11.310 --> 04:16.110
Do you think Aizawa-san will 
actually acknowledge me a little?

04:18.520 --> 04:19.900
Who knows?

04:24.320 --> 04:26.410
<i>This is Jun-kun's real strength!</i>

04:26.410 --> 04:29.580
<i>He said Aizawa-san was stronger than him,</i>

04:29.580 --> 04:31.200
<i>but there's no way!</i>

04:31.870 --> 04:33.290
<i>He's overwhelming!</i>

04:37.500 --> 04:39.750
<i>Jun looks like he's having a blast.</i>

04:40.750 --> 04:43.220
<i>Nothing like when he's up against me.</i>

04:50.850 --> 04:52.850
Don't swing your arm out so wide.

04:52.850 --> 04:56.810
And don't think you can get by 
on just the heat of the moment.

04:58.690 --> 05:01.440
If you want someone stronger 
to acknowledge you,

05:01.440 --> 05:04.990
you gotta cough up the effort, layer upon 
bloody layer, until you surpass them.

05:05.450 --> 05:08.070
There's no other way.

05:10.620 --> 05:12.870
<i>I know I can't win,</i>

05:13.160 --> 05:15.370
<i>but if I can at least get one hit in...</i>

05:23.630 --> 05:24.550
Oh, crap.

05:36.640 --> 05:37.600
Where am I?

05:38.020 --> 05:39.480
In my room.

05:39.980 --> 05:41.360
What about practice?

05:41.360 --> 05:43.150
It's already over.

05:43.150 --> 05:44.230
I'm sorry!

05:44.440 --> 05:47.360
Jun really doesn't know how to hold back.

05:47.360 --> 05:49.990
I really am pathetic, aren't I?

05:49.990 --> 05:51.580
Of course not!

05:51.870 --> 05:57.330
Also... were you hoping to get 
stronger for Carol's sake?

05:57.330 --> 05:58.330
Wha?!

05:58.330 --> 06:00.630
Well, th-that's, uh...

06:01.790 --> 06:02.710
Yeah.

06:03.420 --> 06:05.260
That's right, actually.

06:05.260 --> 06:06.760
So I was right!

06:07.680 --> 06:10.140
Given the way she is,

06:10.140 --> 06:14.010
she's gotten herself into trouble a 
ton of times since we were little.

06:14.260 --> 06:18.480
That's why I wanted to get 
stronger for her sake.

06:19.480 --> 06:22.690
But I've never been able 
to do anything at all.

06:23.190 --> 06:24.320
Like this last time...

06:28.900 --> 06:30.860
I'm just so...

06:30.860 --> 06:34.910
I told you, Senpai, you're not pathetic!

06:35.540 --> 06:38.040
Just because someone's better 
than you at one thing

06:38.040 --> 06:41.000
doesn't make it right to reject 
everything about yourself!

06:41.000 --> 06:43.670
You said that yourself!

06:45.130 --> 06:48.260
Besides, no matter how much 
you train up your body,

06:48.260 --> 06:51.550
the things you can resolve with this 
are things that don't even matter.

06:51.550 --> 06:53.390
There are different kinds of strength.

07:02.900 --> 07:06.280
Ko-chan, you've seemed a 
little more manly lately.

07:06.280 --> 07:08.150
What? Really?

07:08.150 --> 07:08.820
Yeah.

07:09.190 --> 07:13.120
I've actually been going to 
Aizawa-san's family dojo.

07:13.370 --> 07:14.160
Huh?

07:14.160 --> 07:16.830
Aizawa-san's dad is amazing!

07:17.240 --> 07:20.000
Of course, that also makes 
his practices tough...

07:20.750 --> 07:24.210
But I want to become the kind 
of man that she'll acknowledge!

07:26.210 --> 07:27.250
Ko-chan...

07:28.130 --> 07:30.550
How do you feel about Tomo-chan?

07:30.550 --> 07:33.050
Huh? Why do you ask that?

07:33.050 --> 07:34.470
Just tell me.

07:35.010 --> 07:38.350
I see Aizawa-san as... well...

07:38.350 --> 07:39.930
a role model, I guess.

07:40.520 --> 07:43.310
It's obvious that she's physically strong,

07:43.310 --> 07:45.310
but she's more than just that.

07:45.900 --> 07:47.360
She's someone I want to catch up to

07:47.940 --> 07:50.650
and be good enough to 
stand alongside someday.

07:51.570 --> 07:53.570
Huh...

07:57.580 --> 07:59.290
Jun-kun, Jun-kun.

08:00.580 --> 08:02.960
Want to hang out with me after school?

08:02.960 --> 08:03.830
Huh?

08:04.120 --> 08:07.800
I don't particularly want 
to hang out with you, no.

08:08.050 --> 08:10.010
I don't either, particularly.

08:10.010 --> 08:11.630
Then why'd you ask?

08:14.130 --> 08:17.300
I heard you asking Junichiro 
to hang out with you today.

08:17.300 --> 08:19.310
What are you planning?

08:19.310 --> 08:20.600
Oh, you saw that, huh?

08:20.930 --> 08:23.390
I don't know what you're up to,

08:23.390 --> 08:25.150
but all of your meddling—

08:25.150 --> 08:26.310
Hey, Misuzu-chan.

08:27.310 --> 08:30.190
Do you still think everything's 
going to go your way?

08:35.490 --> 08:37.490
All right! This way!

08:37.490 --> 08:39.240
Wait up!

08:41.540 --> 08:44.420
Why did you want to come to the park?

08:44.420 --> 08:46.290
To watch people playing.

08:46.790 --> 08:49.380
Why would you just watch other people play?

08:49.380 --> 08:51.420
Go play with them.

08:51.420 --> 08:53.760
Tomo and Gundo would join you.

08:54.170 --> 08:56.640
I don't think things will
 work like that anymore.

08:57.470 --> 08:58.760
Did something happen?

08:59.180 --> 09:02.890
I said something really mean to 
Misuzu-chan at school today,

09:02.890 --> 09:05.270
and I'm doing something mean to Tomo now.

09:05.270 --> 09:07.060
I'm not...

09:07.060 --> 09:08.980
Don't take Tomo for a fool.

09:10.440 --> 09:13.190
I don't know what you did,

09:13.570 --> 09:17.410
but Tomo's not the type to give 
up on a friend just like that.

09:19.280 --> 09:23.120
Okay, fine. You've got me for today.

09:24.290 --> 09:25.960
You'll play with me?

09:25.960 --> 09:27.580
Only a little.

09:31.800 --> 09:33.130
<i>Why?</i>

09:33.340 --> 09:34.720
<i>Why did </i>this<i> happen?</i>

09:34.720 --> 09:37.630
Wow, so this is your room, huh?

09:38.010 --> 09:40.640
Just leave now. Please.

09:40.640 --> 09:41.510
Nope.

09:42.470 --> 09:46.640
See, the thing is, there's someone I like,

09:46.640 --> 09:49.190
but it's just not panning out.

09:49.190 --> 09:51.900
What does that have to do with me?

09:52.520 --> 09:55.820
If it doesn't work out, 
it's partially your fault.

09:55.820 --> 09:58.490
What? My fault?

09:58.490 --> 09:59.200
Yep.

09:59.780 --> 10:02.120
So I came here to take out 
my frustrations on you.

10:02.120 --> 10:05.290
I'm gonna torture you 
a little. Don't cry, okay?

10:05.580 --> 10:06.790
Who, me?

10:06.790 --> 10:07.920
Here I go.

10:07.920 --> 10:09.460
Have it your way.

10:09.460 --> 10:11.210
Go home once you get bored.

10:11.210 --> 10:12.000
Mwah.

10:12.250 --> 10:14.380
Wh-What the hell did you—

10:14.380 --> 10:14.960
Slam!

10:22.050 --> 10:23.930
Rawr.

10:24.810 --> 10:27.060
<i>Sh-She's scaring me!</i>

10:27.690 --> 10:29.440
Stop it!

10:31.520 --> 10:33.570
I won't do anything.

10:33.570 --> 10:36.990
Why are you so afraid of girls?

10:37.320 --> 10:40.360
You react like that to 
Tomo-chan, too, don't you?

10:41.450 --> 10:43.330
Poor Tomo-chan.

10:43.330 --> 10:47.580
If you keep that up, you won't 
get to be with her anymore.

10:58.920 --> 11:02.050
Jun? Weren't you hanging 
out with Carol today?

11:04.180 --> 11:05.680
J-Jun?!

11:05.680 --> 11:06.930
Sorry.

11:09.520 --> 11:13.650
I just kinda... got hit with 
an attack I wasn't expecting.

11:14.940 --> 11:18.400
What the heck did this to 
a guy as tough as you?

11:21.240 --> 11:23.280
<i>That blonde chick was right.</i>

11:23.990 --> 11:28.790
<i>But I still can't fully 
accept that Tomo is a girl.</i>

11:28.790 --> 11:29.960
<i>And I bet it's because...</i>

11:30.540 --> 11:34.340
<i>We still haven't settled 
that man-to-man score yet.</i>

11:35.210 --> 11:36.550
What's wrong?

11:36.550 --> 11:38.920
I'll help if you need it.

11:38.920 --> 11:39.670
Nah.

11:40.170 --> 11:42.970
It's not something that you can help with.

11:42.970 --> 11:44.720
I mean, we're talking about that—

11:44.720 --> 11:45.800
Hi.

11:48.270 --> 11:50.980
Jun-kun, Tomo-chan, I'm sorry.

11:50.980 --> 11:53.520
Huh? O-Okay...

12:01.700 --> 12:04.490
I'm sorry about yesterday, Misuzu-chan.

12:04.490 --> 12:05.530
It's fine.

12:06.200 --> 12:09.040
But how did Senpai react to the news?

12:09.040 --> 12:10.500
Actually...

12:11.250 --> 12:13.330
I hung out with Jun-kun yesterday.

12:13.330 --> 12:14.630
Just the two of us.

12:14.630 --> 12:15.460
Huh?

12:15.790 --> 12:19.840
We went to the park, and then 
we hung out in his room.

12:19.840 --> 12:22.220
R-Really?

12:22.930 --> 12:24.890
Did you have a good time?

12:25.840 --> 12:28.560
Ko-chan made a really weird face.

12:28.560 --> 12:30.020
You're a frightening woman.

12:30.020 --> 12:33.640
There's no telling what you'd 
do if left to your own devices.

12:33.640 --> 12:35.850
Maybe I should just get you 
together with Senpai already.

12:36.230 --> 12:37.690
You can do that?

12:38.020 --> 12:39.820
You're amazing, Misuzu-chan!

12:40.230 --> 12:43.450
<i>I feel like she's going to 
be the bigger problem.</i>

12:44.530 --> 12:49.580
<i>Carol, have you ever let Senpai 
see you being serious?</i>

12:55.870 --> 12:58.590
Gundo-san, what did you want to talk about?

12:58.960 --> 13:02.260
How do you feel about Carol?

13:02.260 --> 13:03.050
Huh?!

13:03.340 --> 13:07.430
H-How do I... I mean, 
she's like a little sister to—

13:06.010 --> 13:07.890
You can drop that front now.

13:08.180 --> 13:10.890
You love her, don't you?

13:13.890 --> 13:17.350
That's right. I love her.

13:17.350 --> 13:18.810
No kidding.

13:18.810 --> 13:22.110
Your murderous rampage at the 
factory made that obvious.

13:22.110 --> 13:23.110
H-Huh?

13:23.530 --> 13:28.030
And you know how she feels, don't you?

13:28.530 --> 13:30.780
Why won't you give her the answer she wants?

13:30.780 --> 13:32.240
B-Because...

13:33.830 --> 13:37.960
Carol is really strong, unlike me.

13:38.960 --> 13:42.960
I've known her forever, but I've 
never seen her in a weak state.

13:44.010 --> 13:47.050
I thought I was drawn to her strength,

13:47.050 --> 13:50.300
but once I started thinking about 
having that kind of relationship,

13:50.300 --> 13:51.930
I suddenly felt scared.

13:52.470 --> 13:55.060
That whether I said something 
to try to woo her

13:55.060 --> 13:57.440
or pushed her away as coldly as I could,

13:57.440 --> 14:00.650
she'd just accept it like it 
was the most natural thing.

14:01.650 --> 14:03.980
It's not that I want her to be hurt.

14:03.980 --> 14:05.780
I don't, but...

14:06.360 --> 14:08.110
<i>He does have a point.</i>

14:08.610 --> 14:11.450
Basically, no matter how much time goes by,

14:11.450 --> 14:14.200
she's just so dazzling that 
I can't look straight at her.

14:14.620 --> 14:17.080
I really am a sad excuse 
for a man, aren't I?

14:17.290 --> 14:20.790
What do you think of couples who keep saying

14:20.790 --> 14:23.460
that they're going to 
break up, but never do?

14:23.460 --> 14:25.710
Uh, I don't think it's very—

14:24.840 --> 14:26.010
I thought so.

14:26.010 --> 14:28.430
You wish they'd just disappear, don't you?

14:28.430 --> 14:29.930
No, I wouldn't go that far.

14:30.180 --> 14:34.640
But I think a little bargaining 
is necessary sometimes.

14:34.640 --> 14:37.230
She seems to do it on occasion herself.

14:37.230 --> 14:39.690
What? Carol wouldn't do that!

14:39.690 --> 14:41.400
She would, and she is.

14:42.940 --> 14:45.820
You're probably too nice 
to pull it off, though,

14:45.820 --> 14:47.400
so would you like me to do it?

14:47.400 --> 14:49.360
Huh? Do what?

14:49.360 --> 14:52.870
You want to see her in a 
vulnerable state, don't you?

14:52.870 --> 14:55.910
What? When did we get to that point?

14:59.460 --> 15:01.710
Misuzu-chan, welcome back.

15:01.710 --> 15:04.500
You went to talk to Ko-chan, right?

15:04.500 --> 15:05.670
How did it go?

15:06.050 --> 15:09.050
<i>I'm sure she's going to hate me.</i>

15:09.050 --> 15:11.140
<i>I didn't expect this to weigh on me so much.</i>

15:11.390 --> 15:15.010
<i>But this is the only chance I'll 
have to expose her real face.</i>

15:16.220 --> 15:18.230
Frankly, I don't think you have a chance.

15:18.230 --> 15:20.850
Oh, no.

15:21.400 --> 15:22.560
You mean—

15:22.560 --> 15:24.440
You get it, don't you?

15:24.770 --> 15:27.820
You know he doesn't even 
think of you as a girl.

15:28.530 --> 15:32.200
I know you used Junichiro 
to try to shake him up,

15:32.200 --> 15:36.580
but he probably just felt like a father 
giving his daughter away to her groom.

15:37.080 --> 15:39.620
<i>I doubt that will even upset her at all.</i>

15:40.040 --> 15:42.250
<i>Please be at least a little upset...</i>

15:42.250 --> 15:43.500
Liar.

15:44.790 --> 15:47.340
So when they do that, you do this, right?

15:47.340 --> 15:49.880
No, no! You gotta start up higher—

15:50.590 --> 15:53.590
Hey, Carol! It's dangerous 
to run in the hall.

15:59.020 --> 16:00.850
Misaki-senpai...

16:04.650 --> 16:05.940
Gundo-san?!

16:07.020 --> 16:11.490
I told her she doesn't 
have a chance with you.

16:11.490 --> 16:12.450
What?!

16:12.660 --> 16:16.370
I'm sorry. I didn't think it 
would affect her <i>that</i> much.

16:16.370 --> 16:19.330
What are you saying?! 
What happened to Carol?!

16:19.580 --> 16:23.250
You need to go to her house right now.

16:24.000 --> 16:26.750
You should at least... at the very least...

16:27.670 --> 16:30.090
see what she looks like right now.

16:37.930 --> 16:43.270
Did Carol go home early because 
of something you did?

16:43.270 --> 16:44.140
Tomo...

16:44.770 --> 16:47.520
Yes. It's because I was mean to her.

16:47.520 --> 16:48.860
So what?

16:49.400 --> 16:52.780
You can drop the bad girl act. 
Just explain what happened.

16:52.780 --> 16:54.820
Why am I the only one out of the loop?

16:56.450 --> 16:58.370
You're not even going to admonish me?

16:58.740 --> 17:00.620
Hah. Don't take me too lightly.

17:06.500 --> 17:10.050
Um... I heard Carol came 
home from school early...

17:14.680 --> 17:18.470
We'll call this one a draw 
due to injury, Kosuke-kun.

17:18.470 --> 17:19.680
Come in.

17:24.730 --> 17:25.810
Carol?

17:27.150 --> 17:31.480
<i>She thinks I indirectly rejected her, right?</i>

17:31.480 --> 17:37.200
<i>So will she still greet me with 
a smile like she always does?</i>

17:37.200 --> 17:38.280
I'm coming in.

17:43.370 --> 17:44.330
Caro—

17:49.170 --> 17:52.000
<i>I'm an absolute monster.</i>

17:58.390 --> 18:00.970
<i>I couldn't see anything.</i>

18:00.970 --> 18:04.020
<i>No... I never tried to see it.</i>

18:04.350 --> 18:07.440
<i>She's not an angel, and she's not a goddess.</i>

18:08.020 --> 18:11.400
<i>She's just a girl who gets lonely easily.</i>

18:12.360 --> 18:14.190
I'm sorry, Caro—

18:16.150 --> 18:19.570
You jerk! Jerk! Why did you 
come here?! Why are you here?!

18:19.570 --> 18:23.200
Carol! Listen to me! 
What Gundo-san said was a lie!

18:24.450 --> 18:25.500
It was?

18:25.500 --> 18:30.040
Yes, it was! She said it to try to 
get you in a vulnerable state!

18:31.750 --> 18:32.670
Carol?

18:32.670 --> 18:35.840
Gundo!

18:36.090 --> 18:40.340
Misuzu-chan! That jerk! What's her deal?!

18:39.180 --> 18:42.810
It's not like that! I think 
she was trying to help me!

18:43.930 --> 18:48.480
Why would Misuzu-chan being 
mean to me help you?

18:48.480 --> 18:49.060
Huh?!

18:49.060 --> 18:51.690
Er... well...

18:52.020 --> 18:53.070
Tell me.

18:53.070 --> 18:54.480
Y-Yes, ma'am!

18:55.360 --> 18:58.400
<i>Gundo-san made Carol 
hate her instead of me.</i>

18:58.400 --> 19:01.320
<i>And look at how much of herself 
Carol is showing to me now.</i>

19:01.990 --> 19:05.870
<i>I guess there's no way to run back 
to being a coward at this point.</i>

19:08.660 --> 19:11.960
Gundo-san was trying to give me a push,

19:11.960 --> 19:14.250
so I could tell you how I feel.

19:15.960 --> 19:18.880
I love you, Carol.

19:21.340 --> 19:22.890
Sorry it took me so long.

19:28.980 --> 19:32.400
Banzai!

19:33.690 --> 19:37.440
You know what? You know what? 
I love you too, Ko-chan!

19:37.440 --> 19:39.280
Thanks! That makes me happy!

19:40.240 --> 19:43.740
What was it that made you like me?

19:43.740 --> 19:47.120
Um... I never thought about it.

19:47.120 --> 19:48.080
You didn't?!

19:48.540 --> 19:52.830
I mean, you've always been by my side,

19:52.830 --> 19:55.130
and you've always been kind to me.

19:55.130 --> 19:59.670
I don't know when or why 
it happened anymore.

20:00.670 --> 20:02.680
I love you because I love you.

20:05.430 --> 20:06.720
Ah...

20:06.720 --> 20:08.680
Wait, Carol! What are you doing?!

20:12.100 --> 20:13.850
That'll be all.

20:13.850 --> 20:15.640
Boo.

20:19.400 --> 20:22.320
The reason Carol-chan never stops smiling

20:22.320 --> 20:26.950
is because I told her that she 
looks cuter when she smiles.

20:26.950 --> 20:27.910
What?

20:28.120 --> 20:32.870
I said it when she was little to make 
her feel better because she was crying,

20:32.870 --> 20:34.380
but she said...

20:35.830 --> 20:37.040
Okay!

20:37.590 --> 20:40.670
And from then on, she wouldn't cry anymore.

20:41.590 --> 20:43.590
I'm scared for her.

20:44.050 --> 20:47.180
As it is, they say love changes a person,

20:47.180 --> 20:49.850
but if you said anything like 
that to her as her boyfriend,

20:49.850 --> 20:52.850
there's no telling how it might change her.

20:52.850 --> 20:54.850
It just worries me so much...

20:55.350 --> 20:58.860
Well, I don't have any intention 
of saying anything like that.

20:59.320 --> 21:00.860
It'll be okay.

21:00.860 --> 21:05.490
Carol has other important people in her 
life now besides me and her family.

21:05.490 --> 21:06.990
She has friends now.

21:07.570 --> 21:11.750
I think she knows what it means 
to be loved by those around her.

21:12.000 --> 21:15.830
She wouldn't change just 
because of something I said.

21:17.960 --> 21:21.210
That made me trust you a little bit more.

21:21.210 --> 21:22.920
About this much!

21:24.470 --> 21:26.680
Looks like I've got a long road ahead.

21:27.850 --> 21:29.930
Carol's late.

21:30.400 --> 21:32.830
Is she not coming to school today?

21:32.830 --> 21:34.290
I wouldn't blame her.

21:34.290 --> 21:37.520
After what happened yesterday, 
even she must be...

21:41.870 --> 21:45.530
Misuzu-chan.

21:44.820 --> 21:46.620
Wh-What?

21:46.620 --> 21:49.070
She's mad! You gotta apologize, Misuzu!

21:51.200 --> 21:52.290
Mwah.

21:53.290 --> 21:54.680
Thank you!

21:59.240 --> 22:01.240
You lost this one, Misuzu!

22:01.240 --> 22:02.620
You lose!

22:03.010 --> 22:04.470
I have not lost.

22:06.660 --> 22:08.330
I swear...

22:10.850 --> 22:14.600
<i>(This suspicious behavior is...)</i>

22:14.600 --> 22:18.900
<i>Hey, you know, I'm all mixed up</i>

22:18.900 --> 22:23.360
<i>It's too complicated, I'm freaking out</i>

22:23.360 --> 22:25.900
<i>I want to look cute to you</i>

22:23.690 --> 22:29.240
<i>(crazy, crazy, drive me crazy, and that's…)</i>

22:25.900 --> 22:28.530
<i>So I'm plotting, bargaining, 
sly, and stubborn</i>

22:29.240 --> 22:33.040
<i>Dizzying love</i>

22:34.200 --> 22:38.620
<i>Just tell him to look at you</i>

22:38.620 --> 22:43.590
<i>And watch him stiffen up even more, 
because you're both so awkward</i>

22:43.590 --> 22:47.470
<i>What? Even if we're alike in that way</i>

22:47.470 --> 22:52.050
<i>It doesn't make me happy, 'cause it
 means our love is going nowhere</i>

22:52.050 --> 23:00.940
<i>Cloudy heart, swirling emotions—
I sense rain coming</i>

23:00.940 --> 23:10.030
<i>So I partly open my umbrella, 
then sneakily scoot closer to you</i>

23:10.030 --> 23:13.990
<i>Please notice the curl of my 
eyelashes as I keep blinking</i>

23:13.990 --> 23:18.910
<i>And don't say I'm acting weird</i>

23:18.910 --> 23:22.880
<i>All this plotting and bargaining 
is my sly plan to look cute to you</i>

23:22.880 --> 23:27.920
<i>Try to solve the riddle of 
this soft, dizzying love</i>

23:25.800 --> 23:30.050
<i>(Buzzing, fidgeting)</i>

23:30.300 --> 23:34.850
<i>Listen, I might be a bit 
tangled in my own web now</i>

23:34.850 --> 23:38.890
<i>But once you unravel the mystery, 
you'll see pure lo-love</i>
